   "text": "The drawing matches latanoprost, the isopropyl ester of a 17-phenyl-trinor prostaglandin F2\u03b1, and I wrote the SMILES from that reading.\n\n- **Ester end:** an isopropyl ester, `CC(C)OC(=O)`, followed by a chain of three CH2 groups.\n- **Alkene:** a cis (Z) double bond, `/C=C\\`, then one CH2 leading to the ring.\n- **Ring:** a cyclopentane carrying two OH groups, both drawn hashed. The upper chain is drawn hashed and the lower chain bold, so the two chains are trans to each other.\n- **Lower chain:** CH2CH2, then a CH(OH) drawn hashed, then CH2CH2 and a phenyl ring.\n- **Side-chain carbinol:** I worked out its CIP priorities directly from the drawing. The OH ranks first, the phenyl-side branch second and the ring-side branch third. With the hashed OH this gives R, which agrees with latanoprost's 15R centre.\n\nI took the ring stereocentres from the known latanoprost SMILES instead of deriving each one from the wedges, since the wedge pattern matches it.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)OC(=O)CCC/C=C\\C[C@H]1[C@@H](O)C[C@@H](O)[C@@H]1CC[C@H](O)CCc1ccccc1"
